From 24c8b3d98e6ea9979a10af739e019f3dfaa62c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:12:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 107/109] docs: classify route notes match what lemond does
 with a refused directory

The notes said a refused model directory is left out of the model list;
it stays registered, its load fails with the reason, and the server log
names it once. The /v1/classify note now gives the snapshot-repository
exception and says a manifest declaring the image-classification task
makes the directory an image model served by /v1/images/classify, rather
than "not a model". The image_classification_unsupported row names
et-server (executorch) and ort-server (onnxruntime) and quotes the new
remedies. The API reference is regenerated.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
